  "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pdfcpu/pdfcpu/tarball/v0.16.2",
  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pdfcpu/pdfcpu/zipball/v0.16.2",
  "body": "# pdfcpu v0.16.2\r\n\r\nHello!\r\n\r\nThis release makes PDF workflows more reliable: \r\n- preserving document content during processing\r\n- improving forms and encrypted PDFs\r\n- handling malformed files more safely.\r\n\r\n**Upgrading is highly recommended.** Existing Go API signatures remain unchanged.\r\n\r\nRelease binaries were built with Go 1.27.2, which includes important security fixes. \r\nBuilding requires Go 1.26 or later.\r\n\r\n## Highlights\r\n\r\n- **Preserve more of your documents.** Fixes retain inherited page boundaries and resources, shared stamp resources,\r\n  catalog data, and named destinations during affected page, merge, stamp, and bookmark operations.\r\n\r\n- **Work more reliably with forms.** Improvements cover inherited fields, checkboxes and radio buttons, export ordering,\r\n  JSON field matching, empty list boxes, and Unicode text limits.\r\n\r\n- **Improve text and image fidelity.** Fixes address text decoding, font mappings and widths, CMYK image extraction,\r\n  RGBA image import, and compressed image data.\r\n\r\n- **Improve encrypted PDF handling.** Corrections cover AES-256 passwords, crypt-filter selection, extraction permissions,\r\n  and encryption of strings rewritten from object streams.\r\n\r\n## For Existing Users\r\n\r\n- **Validation is more precise.** Strict mode rejects additional malformed inputs. Relaxed mode retains applicable\r\n  compatibility cases and reports notices; it does not bypass every validation or writing requirement.\r\n\r\n- **PDF 2.0 output has additional checks.** Writing fails when required annotation appearances are missing. Automatic\r\n  appearance generation remains incomplete. Standard-font metric completion can also report errors for partial metrics\r\n  or unsupported encodings it cannot reconstruct.\r\n\r\n- **Extraction permissions are enforced correctly.** Accessibility permission alone no longer authorizes general extraction.\r\n\r\n- **AES-256 password preparation is corrected.** Unicode normalization and password-length handling now apply consistently\r\n  when creating and opening encrypted files. Encryption defaults are unchanged.\r\n\r\n- **Corrected decoding may change results.** Applications comparing extracted text or image data should review their\r\n  expected output.\r\n\r\n## For API Users\r\n\r\n- Existing exported function and method signatures, including `pkg/api`, remain unchanged.\r\n\r\n- Supporting packages receive additive exports for catalog entries, standard-font metric completion, and annotation\r\n  appearance checks.\r\n\r\n- Integrations should account for the behavior changes above, particularly stricter validation, corrected extraction\r\n  permissions, and PDF 2.0 write errors.\r\n\r\n## Fixed Security Advisories\r\n\r\n- **[GHSA-ppm7-rg95-2c2p — Plaintext strings in encrypted PDFs](https://github.com/pdfcpu/pdfcpu/security/advisories/GHSA-ppm7-rg95-2c2p)**\r\n  When encrypting PDFs containing object streams, some strings could remain readable without a password despite the\r\n  operation completing successfully. Affects versions **v0.8.0 through v0.16.1**.\r\n\r\n- **[GHSA-gj7c-wpph-xx35 — Process termination from recursive stream references](https://github.com/pdfcpu/pdfcpu/security/advisories/GHSA-gj7c-wpph-xx35)**\r\n  Malformed PDFs with circular `/Filter` or `/DecodeParms` references could cause a fatal stack overflow. v0.16.2 detects\r\n  these references and returns an error. Affects Go module versions **v0.2.3 through v0.16.1**; older repository releases\r\n  are also affected.\r\n\r\nIf an affected version was used to encrypt PDFs containing object streams, review the\r\noutput for exposed sensitive material and regenerate it from a trusted source. \r\nUpgrading does not repair files already produced.\r\n\r\n## Reliability and Security\r\n\r\n- Bound excessive parsing work, reject circular stream-filter references, and enforce resource limits during decoding\r\n  and cross-reference repair.\r\n\r\n- Prevent malformed-input panics involving object streams, cross-reference data, colour spaces, and annotations.\r\n\r\n- Correct PDF whitespace handling, inline-image parsing, effective-version detection, and damaged-file recovery.\r\n\r\n- Strengthen validation across images, graphics, destinations, page labels, and PDF 2.0 entries while restoring targeted\r\n  multimedia compatibility.\r\n\r\n- Expand regression coverage for encryption, document preservation, forms, parsing, images, fonts, and validation.\r\n\r\n## Internals and Performance\r\n\r\n- Reuse validation results for shared JavaScript, Web Capture, 3D, RichMedia, and Rendition objects, reducing repeated\r\n  work while retaining cancellation and cycle checks.\r\n\r\n- Reduce allocation overhead when parsing large certificate revocation lists. Regression tests check preservation of\r\n  revocation entries and signatures and bound allocation counts.\r\n\r\n## Thanks\r\n\r\nThanks to everyone who reported issues and helped improve pdfcpu.\r\n\r\nSpecial thanks to @qoke and the IQ Hive team for contributing the substantial set of fixes behind this release.\r\n",
